<title>JAPAN: Japan's Jusco to cut prices of imported pork.</title>
<headline>Japan's Jusco to cut prices of imported pork.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Jusco Co Ltd said on Friday that it  will cut retail prices of imported pork by up to 15 percent for the  August 6 to August 31 period.</p>
<p>Jusco, a major supermarket operator, said the move follows the government's  decision to exempt some pork imports from tariffs.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the Agriculture Ministry announced that Japan will exempt  some pork imports from tariffs during August in order to lower domestic  pork prices.</p>
<p>Domestic pork prices have risen sharply since Japan banned imports  of pork from Taiwan in March due to an outbreak of foot and mouth  disease there.</p>
<p>&quot;We're going to cut retail prices (of imported pork) by 10 to 15 percent  until the end of this month,&quot; a Jusco spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
